WEBVTT

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.290
Thank you.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.050
I'm John Wyatt.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.320
How are you, Wyatt?

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:04.320
I'm glad you got here.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.320
Be seated.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.910
Thank you.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:13.710
The department ordered me to cooperate with you.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:18.790
The counterfeit money situation in this section has become pretty bad.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:19.680
Lots of it in circulation.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.880
And it seems to be coming from the Mexican borderline.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.220
Have you picked up any clues?

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.750
Nothing definite.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.000
Some years ago, there was an accident.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.900
two men operating a medicine show were caught with some of the bad money on

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.880
them. One of them got ten years and served his time. The other turned state's

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:45.720
evidence and was released. Are those the men you suspect? Yes. We just got word that

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.340
the ex-convict is operating his medicine show again over toward the Mexican

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.480
border in Arizona. It'll be pretty tough to trail them if they slip across the

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.000
border. You needn't worry on that score. Our relations with the Mexican officials

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.900
And I've already made all arrangements for them to permit you to cross the border if your man tries to get away.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.070
You'll have their full cooperation.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.210
Oh, that's fine, Colonel.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.800
Well, this is a new one for me.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.040
Looks like I'm going to have to join a medicine show.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.920
Well, good luck.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:23.580
Thanks, Fred.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:33.270
- Have you seen a show here lately? - Yes.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.850
There was one who got out of here about five days ago.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.950
They owed everybody in town and had to leave in a hurry.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.440
- You don't know which way they were going, do you? - I think they were heading west.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:49.960
Much obliged.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:23.820
- I'll be back in a few minutes, Tom.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.740
- You haven't seen anything of a medicine show around here, have you?

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.600
- Yeah, there was one here, but they pulled out last night.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.420
The sheriff wouldn't let them stop.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.390
He said they were a bunch of crooks.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.040
Which way did they go?

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:36.800
George, Arizona.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:37.970
Thanks.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.390
He busted out his store last night and went out without paying for it.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:07.140
- Better get the sheriff and go after him. - He ain't here!

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:12.870
- I just saw him. - What's the trouble, stranger?

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.480
There's a medicine show here, and the boss got drunk and busted up the drugstore.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.930
Then skipped out without paying for it.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:26.000
The druggist's gone to get the sheriff to go after him and catch the show for the damage.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.410
- Which way did they go? - Right out that way, towards the state line.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:54.110
- You wouldn't drink any more of that stuff.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.990
- Mr. Carter's great boom to human health and happiness,

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:58.420
and you call it stuff.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:07.080
Linda, that remedy has been passed down from generation to generation.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:15.380
The sheriff wouldn't have tried to attach the show if you hadn't gotten drunk last night.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:17.560
Busted up everything in that drugstore.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.180
Well, I'm sorry about that, Linda.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.200
But I'll never do that again.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.120
Not as long as I live.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.510
No, I promise.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.830
- What's that for? - That makes 976.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:42.860
- 976 what? - Time to promise her to quit drinking.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.120
Thanks, boys.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.800
You two get back in there and shake up that medicine.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.820
You don't have to shake it in this tub.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.860
No, you just put it in a bucket. The car will do the rest.

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:03.380
- Hey there! - What's the trouble?

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:08.090
The sheriff and a posse are after you. They're going to attach your show.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:13.050
State line should not be far ahead. You'd better step on it.

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:14.630
Watch the glide, stranger.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:32.220
They're not going to get the old doctor napping?

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:33.430
No, sir.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:37.440
The great brain that concocted Dr. Carter's Indian remedy

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.260
is too much for any small town sheriff.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.200
Yes, sir.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:45.290
You want to remember that the minute we get across that line,

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.210
attachment papers are worthless.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.740
- He can't be far behind us. - I'm giving it everything that it's got.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:29.440
Give a little snort of that Indian remedy of yours. Maybe that'll make it go faster.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:54.190
- What happened? - Something. It's only 50 feet of the line.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.000
- Would you help us? - Sure I will.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.920
I see you're just a little bit too late, ain't you, Sheriff?

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.920
They gotta cross the line. There ain't nothing we can do about it.

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:42.580
Sheriff, what you need is a bottle of Dr. Carter's Indian remedy.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.080
It'll put vehement vigor into that body of yours

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.080
and make you more fit for your job, Sheriff.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.580
Yeah, I'd be glad to take your order any time you want, Sheriff.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:53.290
Good for a man and beast. Better buy your horse a box.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:56.410
Never mind that. You'll need more than Indian remedy

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.840
if you ever come back to this county again.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.860
I want to say thank you for helping us.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.170
I'm sure.

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:18.350
My boy, shake the hand that shook the hand the Buffalo Bill.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:21.130
I'm the celebrated Dr. Carter, world-renowned medicine

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:24.320
master and inventor of Dr. Carter's celebrated Indian

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:26.940
remedy, a guaranteed cure-all, my boy,

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.680
for whatever it is that's wrong with you.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:29.180
Yes, sir.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.000
Every year.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:34.420
Thousands of people come to me for soccer and go away cured.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:35.240
Oh, that's a fact.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:37.070
Here, my boy, have a shot.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.650
Cut out the sales talk, Dad.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.880
I'm Linda Carter, and this is my father, Dr. Carter.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.490
We see I'm passing medicine.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:46.430
And this is Mike and Ike.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:47.550
I'm Ike.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.140
And I'm Mark.

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.880
They're entertainers of our show.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.110
Oh, I see, a medicine show.

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:55.990
Yes, that's it.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.860
And I want to thank you again for saving us from that sheriff's.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:06.850
It's a matter of an unpaid bill. Dad will send it to them.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:10.740
Looks like you need a couple of horses for this wagon, Doc.

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:13.480
Yes, yes, you're quite right, young man.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:14.950
Yes, you're quite right.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:18.950
Looks as though my chariot had imbibed a little bit too freely of my famous remedy.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.700
It's a good thing you came along when you did.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:23.540
Oh, that's all right, Miss Carter.

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:25.920
You haven't told us your name yet.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.760
I'm John Rogers.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.000
- Are you working, young man? - Well, not exactly.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.280
Exactly. I just finished the job.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:34.040
Oh, I see.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:36.680
Well, say, then I'd like to use you with a medicine show.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:40.350
Yeah, you know, after what you've done for us, huh?

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:43.680
Uh, say, can you sing or dance?

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:47.360
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid about all I can do is ride and shoot.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.770
Oh, you can shoot, can you?

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.780
Well, say, say, now, that gives me an idea.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:55.680
Yes, say, we've been needing a new act, you know.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:58.400
Yes, Linda here, she's been doing a dance.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.000
Yeah, uh, suppose you...

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:02.660
and kind of rehearse a little bit and everything.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.620
We'll get together a new act, feature it,

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.000
and call it "The Living Target."

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.500
- Well, I guess that's all right if Miss Carter doesn't mind.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:10.400
- It's all right with me,

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:12.550
as long as you don't hit me too often.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:13.470
How are your nerves?

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.400
- Don't you worry about his nerves, Linda.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.260
My famous remedies will take care of that.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.220
- No thanks, Dad.

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:20.260
I think we can get along without that.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:23.200
- Well, Alma boy, you're a part of the show.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.100
- That's great.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:27.230
I've wanted to join a medicine show for some time.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:29.010
- Well, now that you've joined the show,

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:30.000
I'll give you a chance.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.340
I guess I ought to give you your watch back.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:36.720
That's very nice of you.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:40.720
Why don't you tie your horse on back and ride along with us for a while?

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.920
- We'll drive slowly. - Thanks, I will.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:59.670
Stop at Las Piedras, Aras Rony.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.480
- That's right on the border, isn't it? - Yes, yes, it is.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:06.270
You know, we've never played that town before.

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:09.720
Now, there ought to be some mighty good business down there.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:14.740
- How long have you been in the medicine show business? - Just ever since I was a boy.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:20.730
- That is, except for about 10 years. - Oh, you were out of it for 10 years, eh?

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:25.550
Yes, yes, I had some trouble with a business associate of mine.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:30.000
I took advantage of an opportunity to be connected with a government institution.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.950
- Oh, I see.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:38.920
- You better tell Curly to be more careful.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:39.920
- Well, I'll tell them about it.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:40.740
- Wait till you see our new 20s.

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:43.010
- They're great.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:44.010
- Now, that's what we came for.

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:45.010
We have a deal all set.

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:46.250
Just rid of 500 of those in Tucson.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:47.430
- That's fine.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:48.430
I'll go get them for you.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.350
In the meantime, you boys stay around town,

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.350
but keep out of sight as much as possible.

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:52.710
I'll be back in a couple of hours with the money.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.290
- I'll go get them for you.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.320
In the meantime, you boys stay around town,

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:57.320
but keep out of sight as much as possible.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.660
I'll be back in a couple of hours with the money.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.000
Hey, these look pretty good.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:52.980
Let him in. Have any trouble with that last batch?

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.890
Pete said there was too much red in it, but he got rid of them all right.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:58.870
- All he wants is 500 in the new 20s. - That's swell.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:11.170
Here's a letter from the boys down in Las Cruces.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.950
- Anything, boss? - Plenty.

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:17.470
Old Dr. Carter's heading this way with that medicine show of his.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:21.940
If he sees me here, he'll sure mess things up.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:26.580
There might be ways of making him change his mind about coming here.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:30.000
Yeah, that's right. Take Texan Slim with you.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.150
Okay, boss. Come on, fellas.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:05.120
Well, sir, that's a remarkable exhibition, young man.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:07.440
Now, I think that if we could find somebody

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:09.680
that could hold a cigar between their teeth,

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:16.310
the act would be complete.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.460
Here, Doc.

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:19.620
You hold this man.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:22.430
Stand right over there.

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:24.170
I'll show you my mirror shot.

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:26.440
Well, not just now, young man.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.940
No, we've got to be getting down to the town.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:30.000
Yes, we'd better get started.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.000
Well, you folks go on ahead, I've got to give my horse a drink.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:36.000
Well, you'd better give him a little shock of Dr. Carter's remedy here.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.000
Oh, I think he'd better stick to water.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:38.960
Well, all right, son.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.130
Well, we'll see you later.

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:44.660
But hurry up, though, because we've got to get a show set up in the next town.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:45.660
All right, Doc.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:46.660
All right.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:23.960
There it is.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.440
Come on, Dad. Someone's after us again.

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:42.360
Wait a minute. We were just trying to play a joke on a couple of fellas.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.400
Well, I guess we got the wrong people.

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:47.120
It doesn't look like a mistake to me.

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:51.600
And it's a sense you got the wrong people. Don't forget it.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:15.840
Oh, Dad, here we are, Master Adrian.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:16.740
Yeah, that's right.

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:21.700
Now, if we can just find a place to set the show up.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.910
Oh, look, there's a good place over there.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.320
That's all right.

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:48.050
All right, let's get set up, boys. We're gonna give a show here this afternoon.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.460
And I'm telling you, boss, the cowboy on that show is plenty tough.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.900
Why ride up behind us and take us all off our horses?

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.350
Nothing we could do about it.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.420
But lie out of it.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:15.760
What?

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:17.290
And that's not all.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:19.230
They're setting that show up on the American side.

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:22.850
The game will be up if old man Carter ever sees me here.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:25.020
We've got to get that show out of town.

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:26.270
That's right.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.540
You go across the border and bring that cowboy over here.

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:33.420
- You know, a little money will do wonders sometimes.

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:36.650
- I get you.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:43.810
- There are a lot of things you could do to help

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:45.670
besides just standing around looking.

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:58.220
- Well, I was afraid I might get in the way.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.000
- Bucket in there, mind going and getting

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:20.690
- Glad to. - Well, Linda, I guess I'd better be getting up the street

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:25.510
and let the town folks know that the greater Carter-Madison show is in town, huh?

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:29.950
Just a minute, Dad. Remember that last town you were in?

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.400
Yes, that's right.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:43.060
A friend of yours on the Mexican side wants to talk to you.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.170
- A friend of mine? - Yeah.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:49.530
- Are you sure you're making another mistake? - No, not this time.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.380
All right.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.710
This is the man. Sit down.

00:22:33.260 --> 00:22:35.250
I thought you said it was someone I know.

00:22:35.640 --> 00:22:38.560
Wait a minute. I'm Curly Joe.

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:41.460
The boys tell me you're a good man on the jam.

00:22:41.910 --> 00:22:44.310
Let's cut out the compliments and get on the business.

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:47.700
- What do you want me for? - No, that's the way to talk.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:52.160
- You're working for old Doc Carter, aren't you? - Yes, I am.

00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:55.380
I'll make you a proposition if you're interested.

00:22:55.480 --> 00:23:00.000
- What is it? - I'll make it worth your while if that show leaves town.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.280
What's your game?

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:02.190
No game.

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:04.280
It's just that I don't want competition.

00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:07.590
Dr. Carter's show will draw all my trade away from me.

00:23:07.590 --> 00:23:09.630
No, I'm not interested.

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:12.350
I don't play my cards that way.

00:23:12.350 --> 00:23:13.350
All right, stranger.

00:23:13.350 --> 00:23:15.880
Then I'll deal from the bottom.

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:18.150
You and that show will be out of town tonight.

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:21.130
Or I'll be over there looking for you.

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:26.740
Well, the show always goes on.

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:34.180
So come over early and avoid the rush.

00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:43.610
Now, neighbors, if you will just step down here, a little bit closer to the platform,

00:23:44.140 --> 00:23:47.760
we're about to start the entertainment, my friends, that you come to see.

00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:53.680
We're going to start it off by asking the Texas two here to sing, to render,

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:59.800
soul-started, heart-fluttered and ballad entitled When We...

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:01.810
We're young and foolish.

00:24:01.810 --> 00:24:03.290
All right, let her go, boys.

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:05.800
My friends, the doctors, too.

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:24.420
Young when I dance, dance, dance.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:36.000
They danced with the evening, and in the morning took us home.

00:24:37.070 --> 00:24:42.620
It was in our months, the lights were burning.

